{
  "_comment": [
    "Stage 2 industrial-mask seed: ~60 well-known global heat sources used to",
    "suppress recurring FIRMS detections that are NOT wildfires (gas flares,",
    "refineries, steel mills, persistently active volcanoes).",
    "",
    "This is a curated stand-in for the full NASA STA (Static Thermal",
    "Anomalies) mask layer. Each polygon is a small bounding box around the",
    "feature centroid; sized at ~5 km half-extent for flares and ~10 km for",
    "volcanoes, which empirically captures all FIRMS pixels associated with",
    "the source while not over-masking adjacent fires.",
    "",
    "Sources for the underlying point locations:",
    "  - Elvidge et al. 2016, 'Methods for Global Survey of Natural Gas Flaring",
    "    from VIIRS', Energies 9(1), https://doi.org/10.3390/en9010014",
    "  - World Bank GGFR Global Gas Flaring Tracker (2022 release),",
    "    https://www.worldbank.org/en/programs/gasflaringreduction",
    "  - Smithsonian Global Volcanism Program, https://volcano.si.edu/",
    "  - NASA EOSDIS NRT VIIRS Active Fire FAQ, anomaly-source notes,",
    "    https://www.earthdata.nasa.gov/learn/find-data/near-real-time/firms/active-fire-data",
    "",
    "All polygons are SRID 4326. Box order: [minLon, minLat, maxLon, maxLat]",
    "is materialised as a 5-vertex closed ring per the GeoJSON spec.",
    "",
    "Future stages can replace this with a periodic ingest of the full STA",
    "shapefile published by NASA EOSDIS; the schema does not need to change."
  ],
